Z||000003||jelly2m8||11-18-2001||11:00 PM||||Did you try adjusting the decklid hinges?<P> If you loosen the nuts where the hinges are fast to the decklid torsion rod spring box, you should be able to push the hinges down further. Also you can get a little bit of up-down adjustment on the hinge where it is bolted to the deck lid.<P>An easy way is to remove the engine grills, then do the adjusting with the deck lid closed.<P> the problem in the rear of your decklid is probably because the front edge is so high<P>Good luck||||reg||1
Z||000004||SKIDMARK||11-18-2001||11:27 PM||||Make sure the lip of your trunk isn't bent. Mine needed a sledge hammer after the previous owner tried to put a piano or something in there and bent the edge up. You can also adjust the latch and the catch in the trunk to raise/lower the rear edge.||||reg||1
Z||000005||8Ball||11-19-2001||12:37 AM||||On my 86 2m6 The rear body does not match up right at the door sills. The right is in to far leaving the door frame showing and the left side goes out to far. I am thinking about takeing my body apart to see if I can line it up better.<P>I already need a quarter panel and both bumper covers and door panels b4 I can paint would rather not have to replace EVERY body panel.||||reg||1
Z||000006||tgowens||11-19-2001||03:21 AM||||ok LoW_KeY, now I've got it -- remove the engine grills, raise the decklid and LOOSEN the 13mm nuts holding the decklid hinges to the frame - DO NOT REMOVE THEM! -- close the decklid and while pushing down on the leading edge to the desired height reach in and tighten the nuts. -- the 13mm bolts mounting the decklid to the hinge can also be loosened to adjust fore and aft movement to align the decklid -- just a note here - when you get it where you want it you should scribe around the hinge on the sides of the decklid in case you ever remove the decklid - then you will get the proper alignment when re-installing it.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
